# SOLID Principles

- **S** — Single Responsibility: a class should have only one reason to change
- **O** — Open/Closed: open for extension, closed for modification (use inheritance or composition)
- **I** — Interface Segregation: prefer small, focused interfaces over large general-purpose ones
- **D** — Dependency Inversion: depend on abstractions, not concrete implementations

```csharp
// ✅ Interface Segregation
public interface IOrderReader { Task<Order> GetAsync(int id); }
public interface IOrderWriter { Task CreateAsync(Order order); }

// ❌ Fat interface
public interface IOrderRepository
{
    Task<Order> GetAsync(int id);
    Task CreateAsync(Order order);
    Task DeleteAsync(int id);
    Task<IList<Order>> SearchAsync(string query);
}
```
